  "exe": "allocation-sidecar",
  "issue": "An expense-splitting routine `Allocation.allocate` splits an amount in cents among participants in proportion to their shares. It rounds every participant's share separately, so the shares do not add up to the expense: splitting 100 cents evenly among three participants gives 33 + 33 + 33 = 99, and the group's balances can never be settled. This is the share computation of the open-source app Spliit 1.21.0, reported in https://github.com/spliit-app/spliit/issues/374.",
